(footprint "BNC_Dual_RA_Isolated"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "wl-sync-gen")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Dual-port 50 ohm BNC jack, RIGHT ANGLE, each shell INDEPENDENTLY isolated from the panel and from its neighbour. Amphenol RF 031-6575, customer outline drawing 31-6575 rev A (2013-04-18). Ports stacked vertically at 16.0mm; panel holes 12.83mm at the same pitch, 1/2-28 UNEF. PCB pattern: 4 x 0.89mm signal (pad 1 = port A centre, 2 = port A shell, 3 = port B centre, 4 = port B shell) and 2 x 2.01mm plated, unnumbered ground/retention terminals. Body 14.4 x 36.2mm. Replaces BNC_PanelMountable_Vertical, whose axis was perpendicular to the board (F6). NOT KiCad's own BNC_Win_364A2x95_Horizontal, which commons both shells (it models a FRONT-isolated part) and draws a different manufacturer's body. PIN MAP UNVERIFIED: which port is upper is assumed, not read off a numbered callout -- harmless (independent shells, so no short is possible) but confirm before fab.")
	(tags "connector BNC coaxial dual right-angle isolated panel Amphenol 031-6575")
	(attr through_hole)
	(duplicate_pad_numbers_are_jumpers no)
	(pad "1" thru_hole rect
